{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3311","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3311","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3311\",\"parent_revision\":\"17d6bff5f245b9d2b08be883e876b591e9c0e08376f3f08b761fa53025db03f2\",\"root_revision\":\"17d6bff5f245b9d2b08be883e876b591e9c0e08376f3f08b761fa53025db03f2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe need this serves: keep agent-facing workflow docs from modeling a pattern that looks like unsafe shell interpolation, even when the actual risk is low.\\n\\n**Observed**: `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:98` (added by #3169's CLI-parity work) interpolates `{concept1}`/`{concept2}`/`{concept3}` \u2014 derived from user-supplied title/description text \u2014 directly into a `backlog list --search ...` shell command that an agent is instructed to run via Bash. This mirrors a pre-existing MCP-call interpolation pattern already in the file (not a new class of surface), and the terms are stopword/length-filtered plain words extracted by `build_concept_query`, so the practical injection risk is low. Flagged because it's a Tier-3 prompt-engineering artifact that now also targets a literal shell command rather than an MCP tool call argument, and the doc doesn't call out that the terms must be quoted/escaped when used in a shell context.\\n\\n**Fix direction (from review, not prescriptive)**: note in the doc that concept terms must be shell-quoted before interpolation into the `backlog list --search` example, or show the safer form (list-of-args, not string interpolation) explicitly.\\n\\n**Source**: Surfaced as an INFO-severity finding during the multi-perspective security review of #3169 (content-based duplicate detection), verdict APPROVE.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Multi-perspective review follow-up on #3169 (security perspective, review-3169-20260829T020754Z)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"34e58f1ad479c2c0f8fd77b5be25e3b4a5c3154cb07ac2936813421d4252bd3d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5WtA\"}"}